WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.110 --> 00:00:05.600
I think there's two different types of readers,
people who read books.

00:00:05.600 --> 00:00:09.460
There's the accidental reader, and then there's
the intentional reader.

00:00:09.460 --> 00:00:10.679
What's the accidental reader?

00:00:10.679 --> 00:00:11.679
Accidental reader.

00:00:11.679 --> 00:00:12.679
What's the accidental reader?

00:00:12.679 --> 00:00:14.980
The accidental reader is somebody that just
says, "I accidentally found this book" or

00:00:14.980 --> 00:00:16.820
"somebody told me about it, so I'm reading
it."

00:00:16.820 --> 00:00:22.970
Versus the intentional, is graduated the accidental
mindset and the intentional is saying, "How

00:00:22.970 --> 00:00:26.190
do I pick and choose which books for me to
read as an entrepreneur?"

00:00:26.190 --> 00:00:31.590
I want to talk about that with you here today
on how you should process which book for you

00:00:31.590 --> 00:00:36.140
to read next so you can save a lot of time,
because as a business owner, as an entrepreneur,

00:00:36.140 --> 00:00:38.980
your time is very valuable, and you've got
to make sure you protect your time as much

00:00:38.980 --> 00:00:40.040
as possible.

00:00:40.040 --> 00:00:43.690
And there's nothing worse than reading a book
that's a terrible book.

00:00:43.690 --> 00:00:46.060
So let's go through the system together.

00:00:46.060 --> 00:00:51.489
First of all, for me, there are four reasons
why we read books.

00:00:51.489 --> 00:00:53.030
One is purely entertainment.

00:00:53.030 --> 00:00:57.780
So this could be you like to read certain
fiction or whatever, simply because of entertainment.

00:00:57.780 --> 00:00:59.680
Another one is inspiration.

00:00:59.680 --> 00:01:02.020
I like to read biographies because they inspire
me.

00:01:02.020 --> 00:01:07.970
Oh my gosh, when I read the story of Steve
Jobs or Benjamin Franklin, or Elon Musk, or

00:01:07.970 --> 00:01:08.970
Nicola Tesla.

00:01:08.970 --> 00:01:11.950
. . I just go so inspired when I read it.

00:01:11.950 --> 00:01:13.000
Or it's how-to.

00:01:13.000 --> 00:01:14.430
How to raise money.

00:01:14.430 --> 00:01:15.930
How to master the art of selling.

00:01:15.930 --> 00:01:18.520
How to . . . How to tell a story.

00:01:18.520 --> 00:01:21.619
How to -- all that stuff is how-to to get
steps.

00:01:21.619 --> 00:01:24.000
And then the last one is Knowledge.

00:01:24.000 --> 00:01:25.640
Knowledge could be what?

00:01:25.640 --> 00:01:26.790
Philosophy.

00:01:26.790 --> 00:01:34.420
Knowledge could be the specific details about
health, on how to cut your body fat because

00:01:34.420 --> 00:01:35.850
you read all these different diets.

00:01:35.850 --> 00:01:40.000
I want to be knowledgeable in my diet on how
to become more healthy.

00:01:40.000 --> 00:01:41.250
That's the knowledge part, right?

00:01:41.250 --> 00:01:44.120
So there are four different types of books
that we read.

00:01:44.120 --> 00:01:45.759
Entertainment, inspiration, how-to, knowledge.

00:01:45.759 --> 00:01:51.110
Now this complete opposite side is how I pick
and choose my books to read.

00:01:51.110 --> 00:01:52.210
One is the author.

00:01:52.210 --> 00:01:53.340
What do I mean by author?

00:01:53.340 --> 00:01:56.470
It's similar to an actor.

00:01:56.470 --> 00:02:00.590
If I see Matthew McConaughey in a movie, I'm
going to watch that movie.

00:02:00.590 --> 00:02:03.430
If I see Rachel McAdams in a movie, I'm going
to watch that movie.

00:02:03.430 --> 00:02:09.170
If I see Denzel, Will Smith -- there's a list
of actors that if I seem them in a movie,

00:02:09.170 --> 00:02:10.920
I am most likely going to go watch that movie.

00:02:10.920 --> 00:02:12.700
Same exact thing with a book.

00:02:12.700 --> 00:02:16.121
If Robert Greene writes a book, I'm the first
one reading it.

00:02:16.121 --> 00:02:17.480
Robert's a good friend of mine.

00:02:17.480 --> 00:02:22.330
He's written 40 Laws of Power, 33 Strategies
of War, Art of Seduction, Mastery.

00:02:22.330 --> 00:02:27.980
. . If he writes a book, I'm the first one
that's reading it, because I follow the author.

00:02:27.980 --> 00:02:31.260
So you may read a book simply because you
enjoy the author.

00:02:31.260 --> 00:02:33.480
The second one may be reviews.

00:02:33.480 --> 00:02:37.230
You know, you've got certain books that get
raving reviews, so you're like, wait a minute.

00:02:37.230 --> 00:02:40.790
. . Like, the other day I read a book, and
the reviews are just astounding about the

00:02:40.790 --> 00:02:41.840
book.

00:02:41.840 --> 00:02:44.990
I bought the book simply because of the reviews.

00:02:44.990 --> 00:02:47.200
The other thing may be subject.

00:02:47.200 --> 00:02:50.860
This is very, very important to keep in mind
about subject.

00:02:50.860 --> 00:02:58.060
See, eventually, you as a reader, this is
my suggestion to you as a reader, is to read

00:02:58.060 --> 00:03:01.110
intentionally based on subject.

00:03:01.110 --> 00:03:04.030
Meaning, you are not a good leader.

00:03:04.030 --> 00:03:05.640
You want to learn how to become a leader.

00:03:05.640 --> 00:03:09.019
Go immerse yourself on all the best leadership
books.

00:03:09.019 --> 00:03:11.300
You are not a very good salesman.

00:03:11.300 --> 00:03:13.010
You want to become a better salesman.

00:03:13.010 --> 00:03:15.200
Go study all the sales books out there.

00:03:15.200 --> 00:03:18.250
I get a lot of messages from people telling
me, Pat, can you make a top 10 recommendation

00:03:18.250 --> 00:03:19.470
for sales books?

00:03:19.470 --> 00:03:22.180
I'm thinking about that, I'll get back to
you guys on whether I'm going to do that episode

00:03:22.180 --> 00:03:23.310
or not.

00:03:23.310 --> 00:03:24.530
All on sales.

00:03:24.530 --> 00:03:26.379
You want to become a very good entrepreneur.

00:03:26.379 --> 00:03:27.870
Go read everything on entrepreneurship.

00:03:27.870 --> 00:03:30.300
Go read everything on marketing.

00:03:30.300 --> 00:03:34.720
Pick a topic, pick a skill, obsess about learning
about that topic.

00:03:34.720 --> 00:03:39.060
I have a friend of mine that he wants to study
real estate development, and real estate investing.

00:03:39.060 --> 00:03:40.930
He's reading everything on that.

00:03:40.930 --> 00:03:42.570
That's how it ought to be.

00:03:42.570 --> 00:03:46.700
Social media - read everything on social media,
instead of going all over the place scattermind.

00:03:46.700 --> 00:03:47.700
So subject.

00:03:47.700 --> 00:03:52.989
And the fourth one for me is the credibility
of the recommender.

00:03:52.989 --> 00:03:57.530
There is nothing more annoying to me than
when somebody gives me a book and says, "Hey,

00:03:57.530 --> 00:03:59.440
I've never read this book, but I think you'll
like it."

00:03:59.440 --> 00:04:00.560
That's kind of offensive.

00:04:00.560 --> 00:04:02.800
And let me tell you why it's kind of offensive.

00:04:02.800 --> 00:04:06.780
Can you imagine recommending a movie that
you've never seen?

00:04:06.780 --> 00:04:08.400
Hey, go watch this movie.

00:04:08.400 --> 00:04:12.390
I've never seen it, but go waste your two
hours of your life and then tell me if it's

00:04:12.390 --> 00:04:13.390
good.

00:04:13.390 --> 00:04:14.390
It's kind of offensive to me.

00:04:14.390 --> 00:04:15.390
Right?

00:04:15.390 --> 00:04:19.019
I mean, I like to recommend a book to somebody
and say, I read this book, here's what I got

00:04:19.019 --> 00:04:22.729
out of it, and based on what you're asking,
I think this is a very good book for you.

00:04:22.729 --> 00:04:26.400
That shows respect on when you recommend the
book to somebody.

00:04:26.400 --> 00:04:28.449
So credibility of the recommender.

00:04:28.449 --> 00:04:35.130
So many times, you may read a book because
- let's just say you have a mentor, you have

00:04:35.130 --> 00:04:39.589
somebody that's your adviser, your mentor,
and they may recommend a book to you for you

00:04:39.589 --> 00:04:40.589
to read.

00:04:40.589 --> 00:04:44.430
You better believe if my mentor recommends
a book for me to read, and it's my mentor,

00:04:44.430 --> 00:04:48.849
and they've read the book, I am not even hesitating
about reading this book.

00:04:48.849 --> 00:04:49.849
That book is done.

00:04:49.849 --> 00:04:50.849
Now I don't have a lot of mentors.

00:04:50.849 --> 00:04:53.340
I have a handful of mentors, of live mentors.

00:04:53.340 --> 00:04:57.500
I have a lot of dead mentors, but a handful
of mentors that have influence over me.

00:04:57.500 --> 00:05:00.039
If they come and say, "Pat, you've got to
read this book," like this [snap], the book

00:05:00.039 --> 00:05:01.039
is done.

00:05:01.039 --> 00:05:02.039
Why?

00:05:02.039 --> 00:05:07.669
That person sees an area in my life that either
needs inspiration or needs improvement or

00:05:07.669 --> 00:05:11.360
needs clarity -- that's willing to take the
time to recommend me to read a book -- I'm

00:05:11.360 --> 00:05:17.630
not hesitating because my advisers and my
mentors are more valuable to me than any million

00:05:17.630 --> 00:05:20.990
dollar checking account they could have or
ten million dollar checking account.

00:05:20.990 --> 00:05:24.800
So if they're recommending anything to me,
I will go out there and make sure I move on

00:05:24.800 --> 00:05:25.800
it.

00:05:25.800 --> 00:05:28.729
I get people that message me and say, "Hey
Pat, I want you to be my mentor."

00:05:28.729 --> 00:05:29.729
Really?

00:05:29.729 --> 00:05:30.729
Yes.

00:05:30.729 --> 00:05:34.389
Read these two books - 25 Laws for Doing the
Impossible and The Life of an Entrepreneur,

00:05:34.389 --> 00:05:35.389
then I'll mentor you.

00:05:35.389 --> 00:05:36.389
No, no, I don't want to read books.

00:05:36.389 --> 00:05:37.389
I just want you to mentor me.

00:05:37.389 --> 00:05:40.389
Then you don't understand the subject of mentoring.

00:05:40.389 --> 00:05:46.240
You want lazy way of becoming wealthy, but
you don't want the hard work way of you having

00:05:46.240 --> 00:05:50.479
to click as you're going through this and
all of a sudden you get clarity about a certain

00:05:50.479 --> 00:05:51.909
thing you need to do.

00:05:51.909 --> 00:05:54.499
And so credibility of the recommender.

00:05:54.499 --> 00:06:01.080
So this is how I suggest to pick books to
read.

00:06:01.080 --> 00:06:02.629
Don't just go out there and wing it.

00:06:02.629 --> 00:06:07.789
Generally when a new person becomes an entrepreneur,
you typically read Rich Dad Poor Dad or you

00:06:07.789 --> 00:06:13.650
start off with How to Win Friends, and Influence
People or Think and Grow Rich - there's a

00:06:13.650 --> 00:06:16.879
certain group of books that everybody reads,
and then they get stuck.

00:06:16.879 --> 00:06:20.590
And that typically happens after reading about
20, 30, 40 books.

00:06:20.590 --> 00:06:24.150
Once you've read the 40 books, follow this
system here.

00:06:24.150 --> 00:06:27.800
And my suggestion is that I don't waste a
lot of time with entertainment.

00:06:27.800 --> 00:06:30.990
I don't waste a lot of my time with entertainment.

00:06:30.990 --> 00:06:37.120
As my life started getting busier and busier
and busier, I minimized things that were wasting

00:06:37.120 --> 00:06:38.120
my time.

00:06:38.120 --> 00:06:41.160
If I read a book that's entertainment and
it takes me six hours to read this book, it

00:06:41.160 --> 00:06:47.809
just wasted six hours of my life -- unless
if it's entertainment to inspire my imagination,

00:06:47.809 --> 00:06:49.240
then I'm game for that.

00:06:49.240 --> 00:06:50.240
But if it's entertainment.

00:06:50.240 --> 00:06:51.689
romance novel, what am I trying to inspire?

00:06:51.689 --> 00:06:55.800
Am I having that terrible of a personal marriage
or relationship that I need inspiration to

00:06:55.800 --> 00:06:56.800
read this?

00:06:56.800 --> 00:06:57.800
I don't need that.

00:06:57.800 --> 00:06:58.800
I'm okay with that.

00:06:58.800 --> 00:07:01.199
I'll figure out ways to inspire myself then
using that entertainment part.

00:07:01.199 --> 00:07:05.180
So hopefully this here set up, when people
ask, Pat, how do you choose your books, and

00:07:05.180 --> 00:07:06.180
what books should I read?

00:07:06.180 --> 00:07:10.129
This is the formatting I use, when choosing
books because eventually one ought to go from

00:07:10.129 --> 00:07:13.979
being an accidental read to an intentional
reader to make sure your subjects you're reading

00:07:13.979 --> 00:07:18.889
are progressing in the area of your business
as a CEO, as a leader, as an entrepreneur,

00:07:18.889 --> 00:07:21.050
you're constantly advancing to the next level.

00:07:21.050 --> 00:07:25.990
So, with that being said, if you're watching
this video on a complete different website,

